  "worked_solution": "To find the image of $\\overset{\u2015}{AB}$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the endpoints of $\\overset{\u2015}{AB}:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective endpoints of the image are ${A}^{\u2032}(2,1)$ and ${B}^{\u2032}(1,-3).$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
